    },
    "body": "To protect privacy, the wallet picks a random target for the change output (#24494), inside a set range that is fixed for very small payments, otherwise random between CHANGE_LOWER and min(2 × payment, CHANGE_UPPER).  This function has no unit test at all. You could widen the range, or make it not random anymore,  and every test would still pass. This PR adds a unit test to the function `GenerateChangeTarget`\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>Mutations tested against the added unit test</summary>\r\n\r\n- Boundary change\r\n- Dropped change fee\r\n- Wrong `randrange`\r\n- Skewed distribution\r\n- Halved upper cap\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n",
